---
description: Format rules for task files and the task board
globs: tasks/**/*.md
alwaysApply: false
---

# Task Files

- Template: `templates/task.md`. Reference example: `templates/examples/TASK-000-example.md`.
- Keep every frontmatter key, even when empty. Allowed values:
  - `type`: EPIC | STORY | TASK | BUG | TECHNICAL_TASK
  - `priority`: LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | CRITICAL
  - `assignee`: SCRUM | SA | UX/UI | BE | FE | TEST | DEVOPS
  - `status`: see `.cursor/rules/workflow.mdc` (includes `FAILED`)
  - `work_type` (optional): BACKEND | FRONTEND | UX_UI | TEST | DEVOPS
  - `requires_uxui`: `true` / `false`. Default implied `true` when `work_type: FRONTEND`.
    Explicit `false` skips UX/UI (e.g. Playwright-only). Unused on non-UI tasks.
  - `uxui_task` / `uxui_design` / `uxui_review`: paths or task id; empty when unused.
- `depends_on` is a YAML list of task ids, e.g. `[TASK-002, TASK-003]`. No cycles; ids must exist.
- `requirement_revision` matches the parent requirement's `revision` (empty = any).
- `human_gate` empty, or a reason string; then `/scrum run` waits until HUMAN sets `approved_by`.
- `failed_from` / `failure` used only for `FAILED` (clear `failed_from` on recover).
- `updated` and History times use `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM` from `date "+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M"`.
- Keep section headings exactly as in the template, in the same order.
- Sections are append-only: add `### Round N` / `### Run N`; never edit or delete earlier rounds.
- History is append-only: one row per transition or creation; Note must hold evidence (workflow §8).
- Acceptance criteria are checkboxes `- [ ] AC-001 ...`; only TEST checks them (`- [x]`).
- Product defects also get `bugs/BUG-###-*.md` (template `templates/bug.md`).

# Board (`tasks/board.md`)

- One row per task; it is an index, the task file wins on any mismatch.
- Generated by `python3 scripts/sync_board.py`; run it and stage the board in the same commit as the task
  change (pre-commit rejects an out-of-date board).
- Order rows by status (workflow order, BLOCKED last), then priority (CRITICAL first), then id.
- Columns: ID (link to file) · Title · Type · Priority · Status · Assignee · Depends on · Updated.
